# Known findings for scripts/check-directive-invocations.sh, deferred rather
# than suppressed. Each record names the issue that will close it.
#
# Format, tab-separated, five fields:
#
#   <rule>  <file>  <subject>  <issue>  <reason>
#
#   rule      bash-invocation | exec-bit | shebang | unresolved
#   file      repository-relative path of the directive file
#   subject   the script path as the finding prints it: as the directive
#             writes it, with quotes removed
#   issue     owner/repo#N -- required; a record without one is an error
#   reason    why it is deferred rather than fixed (not parsed; write one)
#
# Blank lines and #-comments are ignored. The check reads this file, so a
# record landing here is a deliberate decision rather than a silence.
#
# Empty: the change that introduced the check converted every directive it
# found, so there is nothing to defer.
